      "post_datetime": "2005-12-05T16:03:00+00:00",
      "post_subject": "Laser Colors out there.",
      "content_md": "Colin, I used to make holograms in Photoresist with a HeCd. Exposure times around 1/2 hour. Of course it was a H1 to H2 with a fringe locker but that was for table stablility. The laser itself was able to handle the long exposures. The only set backs with a HeCd is it's low power (which isn't too back for silver) and it's very short coherence length.",
